===Etymology 1===
From Late {{inh|en|enm|misellen|t=to drizzle}}, cognate with {{cog|nds|miseln}}, {{m|nds|musseln|t=to mizzle}}, {{cog|nl|miezelen|t=to drizzle, rain gently}}. Of obscure origin, possibly a frequentative related to the base of {{m|en|mist}}; or, related to {{der|en|gml|mes|t=urine}}, {{der|en|dum|mes}}, {{m|dum|mis|t=urine}}, both from {{cog|osx|mehs|t=urine}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*mihstuz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihstaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihsk-|t=urine}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*mīganą|t=to urinate}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*meiǵʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*omeiǵʰ-|t=to urinate}}. Compare also {{cog|en|micturate|t=to urinate}}, {{cog|ofs|mese|t=urine}}, {{cog|nds|miegen|t=to urinate}}, {{cog|nl|mijgen|t=to urinate}}, {{cog|da|mige|t=to urinate}}.

